{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler stitch task (#5253) to implement srd021-tac R3.1-R3.4 in the go-unix-utils project. The task requires:\n   - R3.1: Exit 0 when all inputs processed successfully\n   - R3.2: Exit 1 when any input file cannot be opened/read, printing error to stderr, continuing for remaining files\n   - R3.3: Exit 1 when a write error occurs on stdout\n   - R3.4: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   The deliverables are modifications to `cmd/tac/main.go` (extend implementation) and `cmd/tac/tac_test.go` (add differential test cases). The task explicitly says to extend, not rewrite from scratch (Design Decision D1).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (gtac) byte-for-byte via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests\n   - SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for errors\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for locale-independent testing\n   - tac utility: reverse line/record order of input files\n   - Custom separators (-s), before-separator mode (-b), regex mode (-r)\n   - Git is managed externally - no git commands allowed\n   - Build with `go build -o bin/tac ./cmd/tac/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd021-tac.yaml** - The SRD specification defining all requirements. R3 group (Exit codes and SIGPIPE):\n     - R3.1: Must exit 0 when all inputs are processed successfully\n     - R3.2: Must exit 1 when any input file cannot be opened or read, printing error to stderr. Processing continues for remaining files.\n     - R3.3: Must exit 1 when a write error occurs on stdout\n     - R3.4: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n   - **cmd/tac/main.go** - Existing implementation (216 lines). Already has:\n     - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` called at line 18 (R3.4)\n     - `run()` function returns `exitCode` initialized to 0, set to 1 on errors (R3.1, R3.2)\n     - Error loop at lines 32-38 prints to stderr and continues processing (R3.2)\n     - `processFile()` calls `os.Exit(1)` on write error at lines 137-139 (R3.3)\n     - File header already claims: \"Implements srd021-tac R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.4\"\n     \n     Key functions:\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         os.Exit(run(os.Args[1:]))\n     }\n     \n     func run(args []string) int {\n         opts, files, err := parseArgs(args)\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tac: %s\\n\", err)\n             return 1\n         }\n         if len(files) == 0 {\n             files = []string{\"-\"}\n         }\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, f := range files {\n             if err := processFile(f, opts); err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tac: %s\\n\", err)\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     \n     func processFile(path string, opts options) error {\n         var data []byte\n         var err error\n         if path == \"-\" {\n             data, err = io.ReadAll(os.Stdin)\n         } else {\n             data, err = os.ReadFile(path)\n         }\n         if err != nil {\n             return err\n         }\n         output := reverseInput(string(data), opts)\n         _, werr := os.Stdout.WriteString(output)\n         if werr != nil {\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         return nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/tac/tac_test.go** - Existing test file (197 lines). Already has:\n     - TestDiff function using differential testing pattern with gtac reference binary\n     - Tests for R1