{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015J3PRHV6Qvmgqzs6hw1VvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The SIGPIPE test is failing because when a write error occurs on stdout, the code calls `os.Exit(1)` instead of letting the SIGPIPE handler do its job. The issue is in `processFile()`:\n\n```go\n_, werr := os.Stdout.WriteString(output)\nif werr != nil {\n    os.Exit(1)\n}\n```\n\nWhen SIGPIPE is received, the `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler` should handle it by exiting with code 0. But the code is catching the write error before SIGPIPE can be handled and calling `os.Exit(1)`.\n\n\nI need to distinguish between SIGPIPE errors and other write failures—SIGPIPE should exit with 0 per the signal handler, while other write errors should exit with 1. The challenge is that there's a race condition where the write sometimes returns an error before the signal handler can intercept the SIGPIPE signal. at how other utilities handle this... Let me check if `cat` has the same pattern.\n\nActually, looking at the cat implementation, it probably doesn't have an explicit `os.Exit(1)` for write errors - it probably just lets SIGPIPE propagate. The SIGPIPE handler runs when the signal is delivered, which happens when writing to a broken pipe.\n\nThe problem is that in the tac code, it's checking `werr` and calling `os.Exit(1)`. But SIGPIPE is delivered asynchronously - the signal handler should run before the write returns, or at least concurrently. In Go, the `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler` catches SIGPIPE and calls `os.Exit(0)`, but if the write returns an error and calls `os.Exit(1)` first, then the SIGPIPE handler never runs.\n\nThe timing issue is that when writing to a broken pipe, the kernel delivers SIGPIPE to the process, but the write error might get returned to the caller before the signal handler goroutine has a chance to run. I need to look at how `pkg/sys` actually installs the SIGPIPE handler to understand the execution order.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1210,"cache_read_input_tokens":32649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1210},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25451b85-6808-4478-950a-0e4ef670951c","uuid":"a2da73d2-1c33-4c66-9167-e615650e49c9"}
