{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012W3RjKMFUNC55bXF32Ko35","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\tpackage sys\n5\t\n6\timport (\n7\t\t\"os\"\n8\t\t\"os/signal\"\n9\t\t\"syscall\"\n10\t)\n11\t\n12\t// InstallSIGPIPEHandler installs a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to\n13\t// exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching\n14\t// GNU coreutils behavior.\n15\t// R1.5: uses signal.Notify with a buffered channel; does not use signal.Ignore.\n16\t// R1.6: safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine.\n17\tfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n18\t\tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n19\t\tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n20\t\tgo func() {\n21\t\t\t<-c\n22\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n23\t\t}()\n24\t}\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25451b85-6808-4478-950a-0e4ef670951c","uuid":"9ac8b34f-462f-4a0d-ac2a-6df1949c4de4","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:15:16.231Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5253/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage sys\n\nimport (\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/signal\"\n\t\"syscall\"\n)\n\n// InstallSIGPIPEHandler installs a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to\n// exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching\n// GNU coreutils behavior.\n// R1.5: uses signal.Notify with a buffered channel; does not use signal.Ignore.\n// R1.6: safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine.\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n\tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n\tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n\tgo func() {\n\t\t<-c\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t}()\n}\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DGGxefQVnBMwdbFNSuDrrF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issue. The SIGPIPE handler runs in a goroutine - it waits for the signal on a channel. When a write to a broken pipe happens:\n\n1. The kernel sends SIGPIPE\n2. Go's runtime catches the signal and forwards it to the channel\n3. The goroutine reads from the channel and calls `os.Exit(0)`\n\nBut simultaneously:\n1. The `WriteString` call returns with an error (broken pipe)\n2. The code checks `werr != nil` and calls `os.Exit(1)`\n\n\nThis is a race condition. The fix is to check if the write error is specifically EPIPE and exit with 0 in that case, or better yet, suppress the immediate exit and let the SIGPIPE handler take over. Let me look at how other utilities like cat handle this scenario.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":390,"cache_read_input_tokens":34736,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":390},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25451b85-6808-4478-950a-0e4ef670951c","uuid":"90f395b5-e0be-44b4-b22e-e128d5e2bc47"}
